## Durable Generate draft/contract layer (task 2 of staged ontology generate)

Context: Task 2 of the `staged-ontology-generate` plan (design:
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-20-three-stage-ontology-generate-design.md`).
Implements the draft/contract layer only — stable entity identity, the
durable versioned draft, source fingerprinting/invalidation, and the
optimistic-concurrency persistence and validation primitives that Task 3
(staged agent entry points) and Task 4 (async workflow routes) will build
on. No agent, API, or UI code was touched; `agent_owl_generator` still only
exposes the one-shot `run_agent` entry point. The attached implementation
plan (`/Users/benoit.cayla/.cursor/plans/staged-ontology-generate_6fc7e158.plan.md`)
was not edited. Followed strict TDD: focused tests were written and run to
an observed RED (module import error) before any production code existed,
then the model was implemented to GREEN.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateDraft.py (new)
   New, focused module — kept separate from the 2,500-line `Ontology.py`
   per the plan's explicit instruction. Defines:
   - `GenerateEntity` — one dataclass for both the design's `locked_anchor`
     and `candidate_entity` shapes (`id`, `canonical_label`, `description`,
     `type_hint`, `evidence`, `alternate_labels`, `origin`, `included`,
     `locked`). `id` is assigned once (`cand-<hex12>` for new candidates,
     the existing class `name` for anchors — existing classes have no
     assigned UUID and `name` is already the stable identity used
     everywhere else in the ontology) and never changes; `with_updates()`
     rejects any attempt to change `id`/`locked`/`origin` and rejects any
     edit at all on a locked anchor (matching the design's read-only
     Stage-2 anchor rendering).
   - `GenerateDraft` — the durable draft (`draft_revision`, `stage`,
     `source_fingerprint`, `selected_source_config`, `existing_anchors`,
     `candidate_entities`, `completion_checkpoints`). Constructor enforces
     that anchors are all locked, candidates are never locked, entity ids
     are unique, and normalized canonical/alternate labels are unique
     across the whole entity set (anchors + candidates, including excluded
     ones). Review-stage mutation helpers (`with_candidate_added/
     _removed/_updated`) re-run the same invariants on every edit.
     `ensure_ready_for_completion()` enforces the at-least-one-entity
     invariant (anchors always count). `closed_entity_ids()` /
     `validate_references()` implement the Stage-3 entity-closure check
     (excluded candidates are simply absent from the closed set — "excluded
     entities unavailable to completion"). `with_checkpoint()` /
     `next_pending_substage()` enforce the strict relations→attributes→
     axioms order and refuse to reopen a substage already `done`.
     `to_dict()`/`from_dict()` round-trip exactly; `from_dict()` is the
     dedicated migration boundary — it self-heals unknown/missing `stage`,
     `type_hint`, `origin`, and checkpoint `status` values instead of
     raising, so an older persisted schema never crashes a resume.
   - `compute_source_fingerprint()` — deterministic `sha256:`-prefixed hash
     over selected metadata, ready-document manifest identity, and current
     ontology entity identity, list-order independent. One documented
     field-name adjustment from the design doc's illustrative JSON: ready
     documents are hashed by `filename`/`source_hash` (the real
     parsed-corpus manifest contract in
     `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-18-parsed-document-corpus-design.md`),
     not the design doc's placeholder `name`/content-hash wording, so
     manifests can be fed in directly without a translation layer.
     `GenerateDraft.is_stale()`/`ensure_not_stale()` compare a draft's
     stored fingerprint against a freshly recomputed one.
   - `GenerateDraftStore` — the `DomainSession`-backed persistence
     boundary. `save()` enforces optimistic concurrency: the submitted
     draft's `draft_revision` must equal the currently-persisted revision
     (`0` when no draft exists yet); on success the persisted revision is
     bumped by 1. A mismatch raises `DraftRevisionConflict` (409). `load()`
     returns `None` when no draft is persisted; `reset()` discards it.
   - `DraftValidationError` (400, business/structural invariant),
     `DraftRevisionConflict` and `DraftStaleError` (409, optimistic
     concurrency / stale source) — all thin subclasses of the existing
     `back.core.errors.ValidationError`/`ConflictError` hierarchy so the
     global FastAPI error handler needs no new wiring in later tasks.
2. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   Added a `"generate_draft"` key (default `None`) to `get_empty_domain()`
   — the same "sibling durable session state" mechanism as `ontology`/
   `assignment`/`design_layout`, so a draft survives modal close, page
   reload, and backend process restart exactly like the rest of the
   session (the existing `_fill_default_top_level_keys()` migration step
   already backfills the key for old sessions with no code change needed).
   Added a lazily-imported `generate_draft_store` property returning a
   `GenerateDraftStore` bound to `self` — avoids a module-load cycle with
   the same pattern `Ontology.py` already uses for its own lazy imports.
   No other `DomainSession` method was touched; `export_for_save()` /
   `import_from_file()` / `reset_ontology()` are intentionally left alone —
   the draft is workflow-in-progress session state, not versioned domain
   content, and any ontology/metadata change that would invalidate it is
   already caught generically by fingerprint staleness rather than a
   special-cased clear.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/__init__.py
   Re-exported `GenerateDraft`, `GenerateDraftStore`, `GenerateEntity`, and
   `compute_source_fingerprint` alongside the existing `Ontology` exports.
4. tests/units/ontology/test_generate_draft.py (new)
   131 focused tests: entity construction/validation, serialization round
   trip, migration self-healing (unknown stage/type_hint/origin/checkpoint
   status, missing keys), locked-anchor snapshotting from ontology classes,
   deterministic/order-independent fingerprinting and staleness, draft
   construction invariants (locked/unlocked placement, unique ids, unique
   normalized labels including excluded candidates and anchor-vs-candidate
   collisions), rename identity stability, manual add/remove/exclude/
   re-include, the minimum-included-entity gate, entity-closure reference
   validation (including excluded-id rejection), strict checkpoint
   ordering (including failed-substage retry and reopening a done
   substage), the `DraftValidationError`/`DraftRevisionConflict` error
   hierarchy, and `GenerateDraftStore` revision-conflict + durable-resume
   behavior (a second `DomainSession` over the same session store resumes
   the same persisted draft, simulating a page reload/process restart).
5. tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py
   Added a `TestGenerateDraftIntegration` class covering the
   `DomainSession` wiring only (empty-domain default, the
   `generate_draft_store` property, persistence under the
   `"generate_draft"` session key, and that `reset()` clears it) — model
   behavior itself is covered in `test_generate_draft.py`.

