## Address Task 2 review findings for the Generate draft/contract layer

Context: Fixes both "Important" review findings plus two related hardening
gaps flagged against the task-2 commit (`fb35d6b2`) for the
`staged-ontology-generate` plan. No agent/API/UI code touched; draft error
messages remain unchanged and user-facing (no error-exposure change). Strict
TDD: each finding got a focused failing test, observed RED, then the
minimal fix to GREEN.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateDraft.py — `GenerateEntity.with_updates()`
   **(Important)** Was calling `GenerateEntity.from_dict(merged)`, which
   self-heals an unknown/invalid enum value (e.g. a bogus `type_hint`) back
   to a safe default instead of raising — correct for the `from_dict`
   migration boundary, wrong for a live human-review edit, where a bad
   value should surface immediately. Changed to strict construction
   (`GenerateEntity(**merged)`), so `__post_init__`'s validation raises
   `DraftValidationError` for any invalid editable field. `from_dict`
   itself is untouched and still heals persisted data on deserialize —
   the two boundaries are now clearly separated by which constructor path
   they go through.
2. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py — `reset_ontology()` and
   `import_from_file()`
   **(Important)** Neither cleared a persisted Generate draft. A draft
   snapshots existing-anchor identity off the ontology at detection time;
   `reset_ontology()` wiping the ontology, or `import_from_file()` loading
   a different domain/version into the same session, left a draft
   resumable against entities that no longer exist (cross-ontology-reset
   and cross-domain/version leakage) — the fingerprint mechanism designed
   to catch a *changed* ontology never even ran because the caller doesn't
   have to check it before resuming. Both methods now set
   `self._data["generate_draft"] = None` alongside their other
   reset/re-init steps.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateDraft.py — `GenerateDraftStore.load()`
   Hardened against a structurally invalid persisted draft (duplicate
   entity ids, a missing required `id`/`canonical_label` on an entity, or
   any other whole-draft invariant `GenerateEntity.from_dict`'s per-field
   healing cannot repair). `GenerateDraft.from_dict` still raises
   `DraftValidationError` for these — correct, since they are genuine data
   corruption, not a schema evolution — but `load()` now catches that
   specific exception, logs a warning, and returns `None`: the same safe
   "no resumable draft, force re-detection" behavior as an absent draft,
   instead of an unhandled exception surfacing wherever a caller resumes
   the Review/Complete screen.
4. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateDraft.py — `_normalize_checkpoints()`
   Added chain-consistency repair on the deserialize path: a substage can
   only legitimately be `done`/`running`/`failed` if every predecessor is
   `done` (enforced live by `with_checkpoint()`), so a persisted draft
   where e.g. `relations` is `pending`/`failed` while `attributes` is
   `done` could never have been produced by the normal flow. Once a
   predecessor is found not `done`, every later substage (and its result)
   is forced back to `pending`/`None`, cascading forward — a corrupted or
   hand-edited checkpoint blob can no longer let Stage 3 resume claiming a
   later substage is complete while an earlier one has not actually run.
5. Explicitly left unchanged per review guidance: `DraftValidationError`/
   `DraftRevisionConflict`/`DraftStaleError` messages remain user-facing as
   before (no error-exposure change), and `_sorted_source_config()` stays
   scoped to sorting top-level list values only (no recursive/nested
   normalization) — no test in this pass or the prior one surfaced a case
   needing it.
6. tests/units/ontology/test_generate_draft.py /
   tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py
   12 new focused tests: `with_updates`/`with_candidate_updated` rejecting
   an invalid `type_hint` and an empty `canonical_label`; `reset_ontology()`
   and `import_from_file()` clearing a persisted draft; `GenerateDraftStore
   .load()` returning `None` (not raising) for a duplicate-id draft, a
   missing-`id` entity, and confirming the happy path still loads
   correctly after the hardening; and checkpoint-chain normalization for
   an impossible `attributes done` while `relations` is `pending`, a
   cascading `relations failed` case, and two negative controls (a valid
   in-progress chain and a fully-done chain must be preserved unchanged).

