## Staged owl-generator orchestration (task 3 of staged ontology generate)

Context: Task 3 of the `staged-ontology-generate` plan
(`/Users/benoit.cayla/.cursor/plans/staged-ontology-generate_6fc7e158.plan.md`,
not edited). Refactors `agent_owl_generator` into a staged orchestrator
exposing four explicit public entry points — `detect_entities`,
`infer_relations`, `infer_attributes`, `infer_axioms` — on top of the
Task 2 `GenerateDraft`/`GenerateEntity` contract layer. The deprecated
one-shot `run_agent` bridge (`engine.py`) is preserved only so the existing
`Ontology.generate_with_agent()` / `/wizard/generate-async` API path stays
green until Task 4 replaces it; it is no longer re-exported from the
package root and the staged module never imports or falls back to it.
Followed strict TDD: the new test modules were run against a temporarily
removed `staged.py`/`prompts.py`/`schemas.py` to observe RED
(`ModuleNotFoundError`), then restored to GREEN.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py (new)
   Reject-only structured-answer parsing/validation boundary.
   `parse_detection_payload()` parses Stage-1 candidates (fence-tolerant
   JSON), defaults every candidate to `included=true`/`origin=detected`,
   mints a detection-time id via `GenerateEntity.new_candidate()`, and
   deduplicates against locked anchors (and against earlier candidates in
   the same answer) by normalized canonical label **and** every alternate
   label — synonyms are never emitted as separate candidates.
   `parse_relations_payload()` / `parse_attributes_payload()` /
   `parse_axioms_payload()` parse the Stage-3 completion shapes and their
   `*_referenced_ids()` companions extract the ids each output touches
   (domain/range, domain, subject/object) for the entity-closure check. A
   malformed/out-of-schema answer raises `SchemaValidationError` (a
   `DraftValidationError` subclass) — the caller reports it, never re-feeds
   it to another LLM call.
2. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py (new)
   Prompt-first stage prompts (design §Prompt-First Pitfall Handling,
   SPEC §6a): naming rules, entity-closure instructions, and structured-
   JSON-only output constraints are stated in the system prompt itself,
   not corrected after the fact. `build_detection_system_prompt()` lists
   locked anchors (canonical + alternate labels) so the model dedups
   against them up front. `build_relations/attributes/axioms_system_prompt()`
   state the closed-entity-set rule and per-stage modelling rules (naming,
   at-most-one-relation-per-pair, xsd datatypes, disjointness sanity).
   `build_*_user_prompt()` render the closed entity catalog (id + canonical
   label + alternate labels + description; excluded candidates omitted)
   and, for attributes/axioms, a summary of already-checkpointed prior
   substage results.
3. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py (new)
   The four public entry points, each `@trace_agent`-wrapped with a
   stage-specific trace name (`owl_generator.detect` /`.relations` /
   `.attributes` /`.axioms`) and `stage` tag:
   - `detect_entities()` — tool-calling loop (bounded, `_MAX_DETECTION_
     ITERATIONS=8`) over the existing no-reparse `list_documents`/
     `read_document`/`get_metadata`/`get_table_detail` tools, degrading to
     a single-shot call if the endpoint rejects `tools`. A truncated
     (`finish_reason == "length"`) answer gets one bounded "re-emit
     concisely" retry (a completeness retry, not a validation rewrite); a
     malformed final answer is rejected via `schemas.SchemaValidationError`
     with zero retries. Returns `DetectionResult(candidate_entities=...)`.
   - `infer_relations()` / `infer_attributes()` / `infer_axioms()` — share
     `_run_completion()`: a strict-ordering gate
     (`_ordering_error()`/`GenerateDraft`'s `_SUBSTAGE_ORDER`) fails fast
     *before any LLM call* if the predecessor substage is not checkpointed
     `done`; the LLM call passes `tools=None` (completion never reads
     documents/metadata — no-reparse contract); the answer is parsed by
     the matching `schemas.parse_*_payload()` and its referenced ids are
     checked against `draft.validate_references()` (locked anchors ∪
     included candidates only — an excluded candidate's id is rejected
     exactly like an unknown one). Any rejection returns
     `CompletionResult(rejected=True, rejection_reason=...)` after exactly
     one LLM call — no rewrite loop. These functions **do not** persist
