## Fix Task 5 review + browser findings for the Generate wizard UI

Context: Follow-up review + browser-testing pass on the Task 5 wizard UI
(commit `cac2ada5`) for the `staged-ontology-generate` plan. Four blocking/
important findings and five additional findings, all fixed with TDD (each
got a focused failing test observed RED before the fix). No backend route/
workflow semantics touched — every change is frontend HTML/CSS/JS plus one
new/extended `permissions.css` gate. The attached implementation plan
(`/Users/benoit.cayla/.cursor/plans/staged-ontology-generate_6fc7e158.plan.md`)
was not edited.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard-review.js (Blocking #1 —
   draft-mutation race/loss-on-409)
   `postDraftUpdate` used to read `_draft.draft_revision` synchronously at
   call time — three rapid calls fired back-to-back (typing across two
   fields, toggling include while an evidence edit was still in flight)
   all read the *same* revision before any request was sent, so the
   server only ever durably applied the first one; a `409` from one call
   had no defined effect on calls already queued behind it. Renamed the
   function body to `_applyDraftUpdate()` and added `postDraftUpdate()` as
   a thin FIFO-queue wrapper (`_updateQueue.then(run, run)`, with the
   queue's own continuation decoupled from the call's result via
   `.then(ok, ok)`) — each call now only reads `_draft.draft_revision`
   once its turn in the queue arrives, after every earlier call has
   applied its response, and a rejected/409'd request can never wedge
   edits queued behind it. `postDraftUpdate` is additionally exposed on
   `window.WizardReview` purely for the new behavior-contract test below —
   no markup or delegated handler calls it directly.
2. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_wizard.html (Blocking #2)
   Added `data-requires-llm` to `wizardReviewContinueBtn` (Stage 3 runs
   three LLM completions) and `wizardCompleteRetryBtn` (re-issues the same
   completion call) — both were missing the declarative marker the global
   fail-closed No-LLM gate (`permissions.js`/`permissions.css`) reads.
3. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-wizard.css (Blocking #3 — hidden
   pane visibility)
   `components.css`'s shared `.ob-hidden { display: none; }` loads
   *before* this file's `<link>` (base.html's own stylesheets vs.
   `ontology.html`'s `extra_css` block); on the resulting equal-specificity
   tie, this file's later `.wizard-stage-pane { display: block; }` won and
   a stage pane marked `ob-hidden` silently rendered anyway (all three
   panes visible/overlapping regardless of `setWizardStage()`). Added
   `.wizard-stage-pane.ob-hidden { display: none !important; }` — a
   combined selector has strictly higher specificity than either rule
   alone, so it wins regardless of link/source order, and `!important`
   additionally guards against any future higher-specificity or flex/grid
   override on `.wizard-stage-pane` itself.
4. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-wizard.css (Blocking #4 — mobile
   ≤768px)
   The 3-item stepper never wrapped and pushed the row wider than the
   viewport, forcing page-level horizontal scroll — which is what made the
   Configure pane's source tabs and metadata table unreachable without
   panning sideways, on top of a large vertical gap left over from the
   (on mobile, unused) desktop fixed-height/overflow-hidden tab shell.
   Added a `@media (max-width: 768px)` block: `.wizard-stepper-list` gains
   `flex-wrap: wrap`, `.wizard-step` becomes `flex: 1 1 auto` with reduced
   padding, and `.wizard-step-label` shrinks/wraps instead of clipping;
   `#wizardConfigurePane .card.h-100`/`.card-body.ob-tabs-wrap`/
   `#wizardTabContent` reset to `flex: none; height: auto; overflow:
   visible;` — the same "reset the desktop fixed-height chain to natural
   flow after the desktop rule" convention already documented in
   `.cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc` for other sections (Knowledge Graph
   Data Quality, Graph Chat). Bootstrap's `.table-responsive`/the shared
   `.nav-tabs.ob-tabs { overflow-x: auto; }` already made the table and
   tabs independently scrollable — the page-level overflow was the actual
   root cause, not those two containers.
5. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js (finding #5 — focus
   management)
   `setWizardStage()` now tracks whether it has ever run
   (`_wizardStageBooted`) and which stage it last rendered
   (`_wizardCurrentStage`). On a genuine transition (stage actually
   changed, and this isn't the very first call) it moves focus to the new
   pane's heading. The very first call ever — resuming a running task or
   an existing draft on page load — never focuses, so it can't steal focus
   from wherever the browser naturally placed it on paint; re-calling the
   *same* stage (e.g. `resumeDraftFromServer`'s own redundant
   `setWizardStage('review')` right after a fresh detection already
   transitioned there) does not re-focus either.
6. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_wizard.html (finding #5)
   Added a `tabindex="-1"` heading per stage pane as the focus target:
   new visually-hidden `<h2 id="wizardConfigureHeading">`/
   `<h2 id="wizardReviewHeading">` (Configure/Review had no pane-level
   heading before), and `tabindex="-1"` added directly to the Complete
   pane's existing visible `<h6 id="wizardCompleteHeading">`.
7. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js (finding #7 — confirm
   before a stale re-detect)
   The stale-banner's "Re-detect" action (`window.WizardCore.redetect`)
   called `runGenerateDetection` directly, bypassing the "this discards
   your current draft" confirmation — even though a stale draft can still
   hold manually-added/edited candidates the user hasn't acted on.
   `redetect` now points at `startGenerateDetection` (the same confirm-
   guarded entry point Stage 1's own button uses), which sees the Review
   pane is visible and prompts before discarding.
8. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css (finding #6 — gating)
   The generic read-only form-field rule already covers every dynamically-
   rendered `input`/`textarea`/`select` in the Review pane (none of their
   ids/classes match its exemption list), but buttons are never covered by
   that generic rule anywhere in the app. Added a dedicated block gating
   every draft-mutating *button* (`data-action`-selected):
   add-candidate toggle/submit, remove-candidate, remove-alt-label,
   add/remove-evidence, discard, continue, the stale-banner re-detect, and
   the complete-stage retry — `pointer-events: none !important; opacity:
   0.5 !important; cursor: not-allowed !important;`, matching every other
   gated write control in this file. The pane's own visible content
   (locked anchors, candidate list, completion checklist) is untouched —
   only the controls are neutralised.
9. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js (finding #8 — aria
   labels; finding #9 — XSS hardening)
   `loadWizardMetadata()`'s table-row renderer and `renderWizardDocsList()`
   were both substantially rewritten for the staged wizard and injected
   server-supplied table names/comments/document names into `innerHTML`
   without escaping. Added a local `escWizardAttr()` helper (mirrors
   `escAttr` in `ontology-wizard-review.js`) on top of the existing global
   `escapeHtml()` — `escapeHtml()` alone only escapes `&`/`<`/`>` in text
   content and is not attribute-safe (a literal `"` would break out of a
   quoted attribute). Every interpolated field (`tableName`, `displayName`,
   `description`, `file.name`) is now escaped: `escWizardAttr()` inside the
   quoted `data-table`/`value`/`aria-label` attributes, `escapeHtml()` in
   text content. The same pass added the missing programmatic labels:
   `aria-label="Include <name>"` on both the metadata-table checkbox and
   the document-row checkbox (the latter previously had no `<label for>`
   or `aria-label` at all), plus `aria-label` on `wizardSelectAllCheckbox`
   alongside its existing `title`.
10. tests/units/front/test_wizard_draft_update_queue.py (new, 3 tests)
    Real-JS behavior-contract tests via `vm.runInContext` (same pattern as
    `test_no_llm_save_gate_sync.py` — no JS test runner in this repo):
    three rapid `postDraftUpdate` calls submit incrementing revisions
    `[0, 1, 2]` (not `[0, 0, 0]`); three distinct edits are sent to the
    server in the exact order issued; a `409` on the second of three
    queued calls does not wedge the third — it still fires, using the
    revision reloaded after the conflict.
11. tests/units/front/test_wizard_stage_focus_management.py (new, 4 tests)
    Same `vm.runInContext` pattern against `ontology-wizard.js`'s
    `setWizardStage`: the first call ever never focuses; a real transition
    after load focuses the new heading; recalling the same stage does not
    refocus; multiple real transitions focus each heading in order.
12. tests/units/front/test_wizard_review_permissions_gate.py (new, 13
    tests)
    Every gated `data-action` is disabled (`pointer-events: none`) under
    `body:is(.read-only-version, .role-viewer, .read-only-locked)`; the
    gate uses `!important`; every gated action still exists in the markup/
    JS (regression guard against a silent rename); the pane's own content
    ids are never targeted by the gate (view stays visible).
13. tests/units/front/test_ontology_generate_wizard_staged.py
    Extended with 9 new structural tests, one per finding #2–#9 (Continue/
    Retry `data-requires-llm`; the `.wizard-stage-pane.ob-hidden`
    `!important` guard and its source-order placement; the mobile
    `@media` block's `flex-wrap`/height-reset rules; a focusable heading
    per pane; the `isFirstCall`/`_wizardStageBooted` guard's presence;
    `redetect` pointing at `startGenerateDetection`; accessible labels on
    the document/metadata checkboxes; `escapeHtml()` wrapping every
    server-supplied field in both rewritten renderers).
14. tests/units/front/test_no_llm_ui_gate.py
    Added `wizardReviewContinueBtn`/`wizardCompleteRetryBtn` to the
    per-page declarative-marker table for `_ontology_wizard.html`.

